## Updated July 2023

#Problem APEX 5.2.5

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'plots.pl',
    'PGcourse.pl'
);
Context('Numeric');

$a = random(-3, -2);
$b = random(-3, -2) * $a;

$x1 = Compute(-$b / $a);
$x2 = Compute($x1 + 1);
$x3 = Compute(2 * $x1);

$m = random(2, 4, 1);

$a2 = Compute($a * $m);
$b2 = Compute($b * $m);

$f  = Formula("$a x + $b")->reduce;
$f2 = Formula("$a2 x + $b2")->reduce;

$f_int = Formula("$a x^2/2 + $b x");

$plot = Plot(
    xmin            => -10,
    xmax            =>  10,
    xtick_delta     =>  5,
    xminor          =>  4,
    ymin            => -10,
    ymax            =>  10,
    ytick_delta     =>  5,
    yminor          =>  4,
    rounded_corners => 1
);
$plot->add_function($f, 'x', -10, 10, color => 'blue');

$ans1 = Compute($f_int->eval(x => 1));
$ans2 = Compute($f_int->eval(x => $x1));
$ans3 = Compute($f_int->eval(x => $x2));
$ans4 = Compute($f_int->eval(x => $x3) - $f_int->eval(x => 1));
$ans5 = Compute($ans1 * $m);

BEGIN_PGML
>> [!A line with slope [$a] and intercept (0,[$b])!]{$plot}{400} <<

A graph of [`f(x) = [$f]`] is shown above.  Using
the geometry of the graph, evaluate the definite
integrals.

a) [`` \int_0^1 \left([$f]\right) \, dx ``] = [_]{$ans1}{20}

b) [`` \int_0^{[$x1]} \left([$f]\right)  \, dx ``] = [_]{$ans2}{20}

c) [`` \int_0^{[$x2]} \left([$f]\right) \, dx ``] = [_]{$ans3}{20}

d) [`` \int_1^{[$x3]} \left([$f]\right) \, dx ``] = [_]{$ans4}{20}

e) [`` \int_0^1  \left([$f2]\right) \, dx ``] = [_]{$ans5}{20}

END_PGML

$b1 = Compute($a + $b);
$h2 = Compute(-$a * $x2 - $b);
$h4 = Compute(-$a * $x3 - $b);

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
Find the signed area, using the graph.

a) Between [`x = 0`] and [`x = 1`], find the area of the
trapezoid with bases [`f(0) = [$b]`] and [`f(1) = [$b1]`], and
height 1.  (This is a trapezoid on its side.)
[```
  \int_0^1 \left([$f]\right) \, dx = \frac{[$b] + [$b1]}{2}\cdot 1 = [$ans1]
```]

b) Between [`x = 0`] and [`x = [$x1]`], find the area of
the triangle with base [$x1] and height [$b].
[```
  \int_0^{[$x1]} \left([$f]\right) \, dx = \frac{1}{2}([$x1])([$b]) = [$ans2]
```]

c) Split the integral into positive and negative areas:
[```
  \begin{aligned}
    \int_0^{[$x2]} \left([$f]\right) \, dx &=&
    \int_0^{[$x1]} \left([$f]\right) \, dx + 
    \int_{[$x1]}^{[$x2]} \left([$f]\right) \, dx \\
    &=& [$ans2] - \frac{1}{2}([$x2]-[$x1])([$h2]) \\
    &=& [$ans3]\\
  \end{aligned}
```]

d) Split the integral into positive and negative areas:
[```
  \begin{aligned}
    \int_1^{[$x3]} \left([$f]\right) \, dx &=&
    \int_1^{[$x1]} \left([$f]\right) \, dx + 
    \int_{[$x1]}^{[$x3]} \left([$f]\right) \, dx \\
    &=& \frac{1}{2}([$x1] - 1)([$b1]) - \frac{1}{2}([$x3]-[$x1])([$h4]) \\
    &=& [$ans4]\\
  \end{aligned}
```]

e) Note that the integrand is a multiple of the previous integrand.
[```
  \int_0^1  \left([$f2]\right) \, dx  
  = [$m] \int_0^1 \left([$f]\right)\, dx = 2([$ans1]) =
 [$ans5]
```]
END_PGML_SOLUTION
ENDDOCUMENT();    
